  # marks of where a statement stands (tags 40 to 53, nj_mark). Nothing is
  # ever stored into the slot of such a record, so what a function value
  # copied from it was whatever an earlier call had left on the stack
  # there: an address, often, which the collector then took for a value in
  # use, and with it all that value led to, turn after turn. The record's
  # word stays 0 instead. A record's slot is its place among the records.
